# Copy to sanity/.env — @sanity/cli loads it before every command, so this is
# what makes `npm run dev`, `npm run build` and `npm run deploy` work in here.
#
# Both are REQUIRED and neither has a default. That is deliberate: the CLI can
# import, replace and delete datasets, and none of those may resolve an implicit
# target. A missing variable is a startup error, not a guess.
#
# The project id is not a secret — it appears in every published asset URL
# (https://<projectId>.apicdn.sanity.io/…). It lives here rather than in the
# config so there is one place that says which project this Studio speaks to.
SANITY_STUDIO_PROJECT_ID=
SANITY_STUDIO_DATASET=production
